WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:07.838
A card payment of 4.50 hits the ledger, and four parts of the service care.

2
00:00:07.838 --> 00:00:13.691
If post calls all four directly, a broken analytics endpoint makes every posting fail.

3
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:14.837
Turn it around.

4
00:00:14.837 --> 00:00:18.331
The ledger keeps a list, and whoever cares subscribes.

5
00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:22.343
On each posting, the ledger walks the list and tells everyone.

6
00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:24.155
It never knows who they are.

7
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.376
That's Observer.

8
00:00:25.376 --> 00:00:27.332
subscribe hands back a handle.

9
00:00:27.332 --> 00:00:31.308
Forget to close it, and the list holds that listener forever.

10
00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.966
Now analytics is down, and it throws.

11
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:37.951
Does fraud scoring, after it, still hear about the posting?

12
00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:38.761
Pause on it.

13
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:43.911
Only if each call sits in its own try and catch.

14
00:00:43.911 --> 00:00:48.414
Without it, the exception ends the loop, and fraud scoring never hears.

15
00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.380
With it, analytics fails alone.

16
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:56.276
And it's all on the posting thread, so one slow listener slows every posting.

17
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:57.913
Now undo.

18
00:00:57.913 --> 00:01:02.190
Make each request an object: Deposit 100, Withdraw 30.

19
00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.863
Each one knows how to apply itself, and how to undo itself.

20
00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.053
Run applies it, then puts it on the stack.

21
00:01:10.053 --> 00:01:12.139
After both, the balance is 70.

22
00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:15.839
Withdraw 1,000 fails, and never reaches the stack.

23
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.882
Undo pops the top card and reverses it.

24
00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:20.877
The balance is back to 100.

25
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:25.086
Now swap the two lines in run: record first, then apply.

26
00:01:25.086 --> 00:01:26.665
Replay the same three.

27
00:01:26.665 --> 00:01:28.531
What does one undo do now?

28
00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:29.392
Pause on it.

29
00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:39.062
It pops the failed withdrawal, and adds back 1,000 that never left: 1,070.

30
00:01:39.062 --> 00:01:42.107
Record a command only after it worked.

31
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.500
In code, the rule is the order of two lines, in Java and in Kotlin.

32
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:52.123
So, Observer tells a list of listeners, each in its own try.

33
00:01:52.123 --> 00:01:56.987
Command makes a request an object you can stack and undo, once it has worked.

34
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.747
A quick check.

35
00:01:58.747 --> 00:02:04.234
Deposit 100, Withdraw 30, a failed Withdraw 1,000, then undo twice.

36
00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.791
What's the balance?

37
00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:08.122
Zero.

38
00:02:08.122 --> 00:02:11.075
The failed one was never on the stack.
